(23, NULL, NULL, '../uploads/1779619223_ChatGPT Image May 24, 2026, 01_59_25 AM.png', 'CITY CARE	123, Health Avenue, Green Park,	New Delhi - 110016	\r\nDIAGNOSTIC CENTRE	011-41234567, 9876543210	info@citycarediagnostics.com	\r\nCARE THAT YOU CAN TRUST	\r\nwww.citycarediagnostics.com	\r\nLABORATORY INVESTIGATION REPORT	\r\nPatient Name	Mr. Rajesh Kumar	Collection Date	20-May-2024 08:30 AM	\r\nAge / Gender	52 Years / Male	Report Date	20-May-2024	06:15 PM	\r\nPatient ID	CCDC/24/05/78956	Lab No.	2405201147	\r\nReferred By	Dr. Anil Verma (MD, DM)	Barcode No.	:	11478562	\r\nSample Type	Serum / Whole Blood / Urine	\r\nTEST	RESULT	UNIT	REFERENCE RANGE	\r\nBIOCHEMISTRY	\r\nFasting Blood Sugar (FBS)	168	mg/dL	70 - 100	\r\nPost Prandial Blood Sugar (PPBS)	245	mg/dL	< 140	\r\nHbA1c	8.7	4.0 - 5.6	\r\nMethod: HPLC	\r\nSerum Creatinine	1.8	mg/dL	0.7 - 1.2	\r\nBlood Urea Nitrogen (BUN)	32	mg/dL	7 - 20	\r\nSerum Uric Acid	7.9	mg/dL	3.5 - 7.2	\r\nTotal Cholesterol	252	mg/dL	< 200	\r\nLDL Cholesterol	162	mg/dL	< 100	\r\nHDL Cholesterol	34	mg/dL	> 40	\r\nTriglycerides	236	mg/dL	< 150	\r\nURINE EXAMINATION	\r\nSugar (Urine)	2+	Negative	\r\nProtein (Urine)	1+	Negative	\r\nMicroalbumin (Urine)	112	mg/L	< 30	\r\nMethod: Immunoturbidimetry	\r\nCOMPLETE BLOOD COUNT (CBC)	\r\nHemoglobin	13.2	g/dL	13.0 - 17.0	\r\nTotal Leucocyte Count (TLC)	8,600	/uL	4,000 - 11,000	\r\nPlatelet Count	2,10,000	/uL	1,50,000 - 4,00,000	\r\n* Red values indicate abnormal hich | Blue values indicate abnormal low	\r\nINTERPRETATION:	\r\n• FBS, PPBS and HbA1c are HIGH - consistent with POOR GLYCEMIC CONTROL.	\r\n• Serum Creatinine, BUN and Urine Microalbumin are HIGH - suggestive of DIABETIC NEPHROPATHY.	\r\n• Lipid profile shows HIGH LDL, HIGH Triglycerides and LOW HDL - increased risk of CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE.	\r\n• Urine shows presence of Sugar and Protein - early signs of kidney involvement.	\r\nCLINICAL CORRELATION:	\r\nThe findings are suggestive of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus with poor glycemic control and early diabetic nephropathy.	\r\nDyslipidemia is present. Kindly correlate clinically and manage accordingly.	\r\nTHEORY / INFORMATION:	\r\nDiabetes Mellitus is a chronic metabolic disorder characterized by hyperglycemia resulting from defects in insulin secretion,	\r\ninsulin action or both. Persistent hyperglycemia can lead to microvascular complications (retinopathy, nephropathy,	\r\nneuropathy) and macrovascular complications (coronary artery disease, stroke, peripheral vascular disease).	\r\nHbA1c reflects average blood glucose over previous 2-3 months. Target HbA1c for most adults is < 7.0%.	\r\nNote:	Rehona	DIAGNOST	\r\n• This report relates only to the sample tested.	CARE	QUALITY	\r\n• Correlate clinically. Repeat test if necessary.	Dr. Neha Sharma	YOU CAN	\r\n• Not for medico-legal purpose.	TRUST	\r\nMD (Pathology)	\r\n--- End of Report --	Consultant Pathologist	\r\nReg. No.: DMC/2010/56214	\r\n', NULL, 346, 2732, '2026-05-24 03:40:28'),
