(26, NULL, NULL, '../uploads/1779620396_ChatGPT Image May 24, 2026, 02_15_26 AM.png', '25, Health City, Park Road,	\r\nLIFELINE DIAGNOSTIC CENTRE	New Delhi - 110016	\r\n011-41234567	\r\nAccuracy | Care | Compassion	\r\ninfo@lifelinediagnostics.com	\r\nBLOOD INVESTIGATION REPORT	\r\nPatient Name : Rajesh Kumar	Report No.	: LLDC/24/05/7896	\r\nAge / Gender	: 46 Years / Male	Date of Collection: 20-May-2024 20-May-2024 AM	\r\nPatient ID	: LLDC/24/05/7896	Date of Reporting: 20-May-2024 05:45 PM	\r\nReferred By : Dr. Anil Verma (MD)	Lab No.	: 2405201147	\r\nSample Type: Whole Blood	\r\nTEST	RESULT	UNIT	REFERENCE RANGE	\r\nFasting Blood Sugar (FBS)	168	1	mg/dL	70 - 100	\r\nHemoglobin (Hb)	11.2	g/dL	13.0 - 17.0	\r\nNote: T High Low	\r\nINTERPRETATION:	\r\n• Fasting Blood Sugar is HIGH - suggests poor glycemic control / possible Diabetes Mellitus.	\r\n• Hemoglobin is LOW - suggests mild anemia.	\r\nTHEORY / INFORMATION:	\r\n1. BLOOD SUGAR (GLUCOSE)	\r\nGlucose is the primary source of energy for the body. It comes from the food we eat and is regulated by the hormone	\r\ninsulin produced by the pancreas. When blood sugar is high for a long time, it can damage blood vessels, nerves,	\r\nkidneys, eyes and heart.	\r\n• Normal Fasting Blood Sugar: 70 - 100 mg/dL	\r\n• Prediabetes: 100 - 125 mg/dL	\r\n• Diabetes: ≥ 126 mg/dL	\r\n2. HEMOGLOBIN (Hb)	\r\nHemoglobin is a protein in red blood cells that carries oxygen from the lungs to all parts of the body.	\r\nLow hemoglobin means the body may not get enough oxygen, leading to tiredness, weakness, dizziness	\r\nand shortness of breath.	\r\n• Normal Hb (Male): 13.0 - 17.0 g/dL	\r\n• Mild Anemia: 10.0 - 13.0 g/dL	\r\n• Moderate Anemia: 7.0 - 10.0 g/dL	\r\n• Severe Anemia: < 7.0 g/dL	\r\nGENERAL ADVICE:	\r\n• Follow a balanced diet low in sugar and refined carbohydrates.	\r\n• Exercise regularly and maintain healthy body weight.	\r\n• Eat iron-rich foods (green leafy vegetables, pulses, jaggery, dates) to improve hemoglobin.	\r\n• Drink plenty of water and avoid smoking & alcohol.	\r\n• Repeat test and follow up with your physician.	\r\nRehan	\r\nDr. Neha Sharma	\r\nChecked By:	MD (Pathology)	15E	\r\nConsultant Pathologist	\r\nLab Technician	*** End of Report ***	Reg. No.: DMC/2010/56214	\r\n', NULL, 292, 2114, '2026-05-24 04:00:01'),
