(41, 58, NULL, '../uploads/1781175071_Screenshot 2026-06-11 at 03.50.44.png', 'Medical Report Letter from Doctor	\r\n[Your Name]	\r\nPhysician	\r\n[Your Company Name]	\r\nDate: 10/04/2050	\r\nClint Renner	\r\nPatient Relations Coordinator	\r\n[Your Company Name]	\r\nDear Clint Renner,	\r\nI am writing to provide a comprehensive medical report regarding my patient, Elvie Block, who	\r\nwas examined on September 28, 2050, for concerns related to persistent headaches. The	\r\nfollowing outlines the findings, diagnosis, and treatment plan:	\r\nPatient Information	\r\n• Patient Name: Elvie Block	\r\n• Date of Birth: March 15, 1985	\r\n• Gender: Female	\r\n• Patient ID: HS987654	\r\nMedical History	\r\nThe patient has a significant medical history, which includes:	\r\n• Migraine headaches	\r\n• No known allergies	\r\n• Currently taking Ibuprofen as needed	\r\nExamination Findings	\r\nUpon examination, the following findings were noted:	\r\n• Vital Signs: Blood Pressure 120/80 mmHg, Heart Rate 72 bpm	\r\n• Physical Examination Findings: Alert, oriented, mild temporal tenderness	\r\nDiagnostic Tests	\r\nLaboratory tests and imaging studies were performed, including:	\r\n• MRI of the brain: No abnormalities detected	\r\n• Complete Blood Count: Within normal limits	\r\n', NULL, 141, 1163, '2026-06-11 03:51:15'),
(42, 58, NULL, '../uploads/1781175389_Screenshot 2026-06-11 at 03.56.24.png', '123, Health Care Road,	\r\nCARE WELL	Bangalore - 560068, Karnataka	\r\nPh: 080-12345678	\r\nMULTISPECIALITY HOSPITAL	\r\nEmail: info@carewellhospital.com	\r\nCT SCAN REPORT	\r\nPatient Name: Rahul Verma	Study Date	: 10/06/2026	\r\nPatient ID	: C/25/48752	Report Date	: 11/06/2026	\r\nAge / Gender: 52 Years / Male	Modality	: CT	\r\nReferred By	: Dr. Anil Sharma	Study Type	: CT Thorax (Plain + Contrast)	\r\nCLINICAL HISTORY:	\r\nChronic cough with breathlessness since 2 months.	\r\nFINDINGS:	\r\n• A well-defined lobulated soft tissue lesion is seen in the right upper lobe	\r\nmeasuring approx. 3.2 x 2.7 cm showing mild post-contrast enhancement.	\r\n• Multiple enlarged lymph nodes are noted in the right paratracheal	\r\nand subcarinal regions, largest measuring 1.8 x 1.2 cm.	\r\n• Mild centrilobular emphysematous changes seen in bilateral lung fields.	\r\n• No evidence of pleural effusion.	\r\n• Trachea and major bronchi appear normal.	\r\n• Visualized bones show no obvious lytic or sclerotic lesion.	\r\nIMPRESSION:	\r\n1. Well-defined enhancing lesion in right upper lobe - likely neoplastic etiology.	\r\n2. Mediastinal lymphadenopathy - likely metastatic.	\r\n3. Mild bilateral emphysematous changes.	\r\nRECOMMENDATION: Clinical correlation and biopsy correlation advised.	\r\n*** End Of Report ***	\r\npliesce	Raghaw n	\r\nDr. Meera lyer	Dr. Raghav Menon	\r\nMD (Radiodiagnosis)	MD (Radiodiagnosis)	\r\nKMC No: 75934	KMC No: 62145	\r\nDISCLAIMER:	\r\nThis report is based on the imaging findings and should be correlated clinically.	\r\nNot valid for medico-legal purpose.	\r\n', NULL, 190, 1539, '2026-06-11 03:56:34'),
