(100, 58, NULL, '../uploads/1786369925_Screenshot 2026-08-10 at 06.52.02.png', '* Sample Letterhead\nyourlabname@-gmail.com\n• https://wwwyourlabname.in/\nMrs. Sha Bosco\nAge / Sex\n: 98 YRS /F\nReterred by : Self\nReg. no.\n: 1003\nTEST\nBUN\nSERUM UREA\nSERUM CREATININE\nEGFR\nMethod: Calculated\nEGFR CATEGORY\nMethod Calculated\nSERUM CALCIUM\nSERUM POTASSIUM\nSERUM SODIUM\nSERUM URIC ACID\nUREA / CREATININE RATIO\nBUN / CREATININE RATIO\n1003\nRegistered on: 16/10/2024 05:28 PM\nCollected on : 16/10/2024\nReceived on : 16/102024\nReported on\n: 16/10/2024 05:31 PM\nBIOCHEMISTRY\nKIDNEY FUNCTION TEST (KFT)\nVALUE\n10.27\n22\nUNIT\nmg/di\nmg/dl\n1.01\nL\n50.32\nREFERENCE\n7.9-20\n21 - 43\n0.55 - 1.02\nml/min/1.73m^2\n> 90\nG3a\n92\n3.6\n138\n4\n21.78\n10.17\nmgidl\nmmol/L\nmmol/L\nmgidl\n8.8 - 10.6\n3.5 - 5.1\n136 - 146\n2.6 - 6\nCreatinine is a nitrogenous waste product formed in muscle from creatine phosphate. Endogenous production of creatinine is\nproportional to muscle mass and body weight.\nCauses of Increased Serum Creatinine Level\nCauses of Decreased Serum Creatinine Level\n1. Pre-renal, renal, and post-renal azotemia\n2. Large amount of dietary meat\n1. Pregnancy\n2. Increasing age (reduction in muscle mass)\n3. Active acromegaly and gigantism\nGFRis measured to (i) detect suspected incipient kidney disease (i,e. early detection), (il)monitor the course of established\nkidney disease, (i) plan renal replacement therapy in advanced renal disease, and (iv) adjust the dosage of certain drugs\nwhich are nephrotoxic.\nBUN/creatinine ratio is to discriminate pre-renal and post-renal azotemia from renal azotemia.\n- End of report -\nSachie\nMr. Sachin Sharma\nAk Astor\nDr. A. K. Asthana', NULL, 215, 1564, '2026-08-10 06:52:16'),
(101, 58, NULL, '../uploads/1786370028_Screenshot 2026-08-10 at 06.53.42.png', 'TEST	RESULTS	\r\nName: Kevin Beck	Age: 23 years old	\r\nDate: 2023-02-06	Sex: Male	\r\nPatient #: 037424	Test ID: 0994-2341	\r\nTest	Results	Reference Range	\r\nComplete Blood Count	\r\nWhite cells blood	5.6 × 109 / L	4.0 - 10.0	\r\nHemoglobin	190 × 109 / L	350 - 350	\r\nBlood Chemistry	\r\nProtein	68g/L	66 - 83	\r\nAlbumin	41g/L	35 - 52	\r\nCreatinine	116.7 umol/L	44.2 - 79.6	\r\nCalcium	2.2 mmol/L	2.2 - 27	\r\nPhosphorus	1.2 mmol/L	0.8 - 1.5	\r\nSodium	140 mmol/L	136 - 146	\r\nPotasium	3.9 mmol/L	3.5 - 5.1	\r\nChloride	103 mmol/L	101 - 109	\r\nUric Acid	203.2 umol/L	101 - 109	\r\nBlood Urea Nitrogen	5.4 mmol/L	154.7 - 35.9	\r\nlg G	13.2 g/L	2.86 - 7.14	\r\nIg A	890 mg/L	0.7 - 1.6	\r\nlg M	650 mh/L	700 - 4000	\r\n', NULL, 92, 682, '2026-08-10 06:53:55');

